<h1>Inverse</h1>
<hr align="center" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from the</span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>tree context menu</b></span> <span class="Path">for</span> <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Transformation &gt; Inverse</b></span></i><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Inverse</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command inverses the transformation matrix of a transformation. The inverse of a square matrix <b>A</b>, sometimes called reciprocal matrix, is a matrix <b>A<sup>-1</sup></b> such that <b>AA<sup>-1</sup></b> = <b>I</b>, where <b>I</b> is the identity matrix.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">In case of</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>4x4</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">matrix <b>I</b> has the following form:</span></p>
<table cellspacing="0" class="whs4">
<col>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td class="whs6">
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><sub style="vertical-align:sub;"><img src="../view_menu/Using_Datums_files/image089.gif" width="89px" height="91px" align="left" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></sub></span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;">&#160;</p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB">A square matrix <b>A</b> has an inverse if the determinant |<b>A</b>|</span> <span style="font-family:Symbol;"><img src="../view_menu/Using_Datums_files/Image002.gif" width="7px" height="10px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""></span> <span lang="EN-GB">0. A matrix possessing an inverse is called nonsingular, or invertible.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP226203994" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<table cellspacing="5" class="whs9">
<col>
<col>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td class="whs10">
<p><img src="Images/image3.jpg" width="421px" height="307px" border="0" class="img_whs11" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td class="whs12">
<p><img src="Images/image4.jpg" width="421px" height="307px" border="0" class="img_whs13" alt=""></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td class="whs14">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Transformation matrix</span></p>
</td>
<td class="whs15">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Inverted transformation matrix</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p>&#160;</p>
</div>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">When use</span> <span class="Command">Apply Reverse</span> <span lang="EN-GB">the inverted matrix of the transformation is applied to the selected entities, but its matrix remains unchanged. The difference here is that</span> <span class="Command">Inverse</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command modifies the matrix of the transformation without applying any transformations to the objects.</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Related topic:</b></span> <u style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB&quot;"><a href="apply_reverse.htm">Apply Reverse</a></span></u><span lang="EN-GB">&#160;</span></p>
